{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact member/presence design e00abdb700de3a0a5d6977a30c915c6428871a9d, tree db8b2d3bdcccdf41a614c2f85b9a118ea0e08f30.\n\nF1 (P1), primary141–146,166–172,228–235: define the recorded stand-in's state/completeness contract before promising current room occupancy from today's Grow events. On this head, Site.arrive/leave are signed comment acts with no effects and only a room item field. The maintained presence projection is a log of the last100 native entries, filters arrive/leave, uses latestBy:null, and exposes actor+room; it has no about field or complete current-presence state. The overview does not already establish who is currently in every room. Selecting a latest actor within that tail cannot recover someone whose last relevant event preceded it, and an omitted actor is not a proved departure.\n\nA focused probe with the maintained Site definition, actual pure judges/folds and production journal projector records Rita.arrive at2, then100 Una.leave events through head102. The complete returned native window starts3 and has100 rows, zero Rita rows, while the full journal contains Rita's arrival and no Rita departure. Probe /private/tmp/checker-m2a-interface-2xdpvocs/repo/checker-recorded-presence-window.mts; report /private/tmp/checker-m2a-interface-2xdpvocs/recorded-presence-window-validation.json. TEST in-memory authority and an undelivered Room creation remain labelled; no native install/live presence claim.\n\nChoose a bounded supported source for B3: either explicit recorded presence items/another complete materialization with its owning acts and readable subject mapping, or a recent-event stand-in labelled as recent reported activity with unknown state outside its window. Specify room item→full subject/about binding, latest/leave/multiple-room semantics and partial/absent/unavailable expressions. Commission any Grow schema/projection change that this needs rather than claim the current log is a complete occupancy source. Preserve no lease/status/freshness claims for recorded activity, and keep G3 routing/live attention deferred. Add a witness with the last relevant event outside the window and a late-opening client; do not repair this with an unbounded historical scan.\n\nF2 (P2),71 and101–111: the fixed expression “removed, since entry N” has no stated bounded source for N. Native Item holds id/opened (the opening fact), state and item revision; it has no last-state-change sequence or removedAt fact (packages/contract/src/read.ts41–58). Membership.remove-member changes state only, and the ordinary Summary omits final items. The resolver's listed admitted-entry field identifies joining/opening, not removal. Neither item.id, item.revision nor the membership's current head is the removal position. State a checked bounded provenance read or index for that label, with its budget and unavailable case, or use “removed” when its removal fact cannot be read. Retain known identity/state when only this optional provenance is unavailable. Add a removed-member example whose transition is outside the recent journal window.\n\nImplementation fidelity: Read all262 primary lines first, then the relevant membership, projection grammar/projector, current Grow presence declaration, kit source/tool/session boundaries and the inherited volatile presence/session/lease contract. All2240 regular Git leaves/modes/blob IDs were verified. Against authored Main4d8c878c4c40f6d4399f2bcf5567125bb3ba1bc8/treee568c5d498e974bacd49e135e452e8b5a24edbee only this note changes and2239 leaves are unchanged; whitespace check passes.\n\nCorrectness/verification: The three-layer split, explicit unavailable identity/standing, raw-ref fallback, controller attribution,32-member/byte caps, kit-only standing controls and package member-open-only API are sound directions. Existing party and journal signer field kinds supply typed native member refs; they do not themselves supply display names, current presence or lifecycle event positions. The inherited live declaration requires actual Enter/Renew/Leave judgments with current action/session ownership/generation/expected checks; app-only visibility or a read token alone is no write authority. Auto renewal is B4, not a capability already provided by view_read, and the reset/lease-end rules remain required. Kit-owned controls are an API authority boundary to implement and test, not hostile-script isolation supplied by today's trusted inline surface.\n\nEvidence limits: Design-only review; no source/tests changed, so docs/testing.md's documentation-only exception applies and no full gate was repeated. My probe shows a bounded log's information limit, not a complete member resolver or live executor. D1 mockups and B1–B4 implementation, native authority/custody/read revalidation, absent/final-member cases, overflow/controller cases, stale callbacks, reset/disconnect/lease expiry, and actual browser acceptance remain owed. No provider, deployment, publication, native-device or hostile-code isolation claim.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:4df0afbe2a024d7dd6bc94a99333bcefe8c06f95","binding":"assigned","head":"e00abdb700de3a0a5d6977a30c915c6428871a9d","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:48b3fa152f141d425a1b91f4dea96c5b81c7f8c9\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:45d75285ba181142cec9f66a640987a0b44093bc\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9493bc5ab0791a26679765c2d53b0cf1be24ed15","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}